ge": "english", "persons": [], "text": "Oracle continued its recent rally. More Investing.com - Technology stocks led the rally midday, rebounding from weakness in the previous day led by software and chip stocks.\nThe Nasdaq Composite rose about 1% at 12:00 PM ET (16:00 GMT), while the S&P Information Technology index gained about 1.2%.\nOracle (NYSE:ORCL) climbed about 3%, continuing its post-earnings comeback. Oracle reported numbers on Monday, with revenue coming in shy of expectations, but after the knee-jerk drop, the stock has rallied sharply. Microsoft (NASDAQ:MSFT) shares gained about 1.4%.\nMeanwhile, semiconductor stocks were mostly higher ahead of Micron Technology’s earnings report after the bell.\nMicron (NASDAQ:MU) rose about 2.5% and Intel (NASDAQ:INTC) was up around 2%.\nNVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) was the notable exception, sinking about 2.5%.\nMicron should give investors more clarity on whether memory chips are moving into a downward cycle .\nAmong the FAANG stocks, Facebook (NASDAQ:FB), Amazon (NASDAQ:AMZN), Apple (NASDAQ:AAPL) and Google parent Alphabet (NASDAQ:GOOGL) were all up around 1%, with only Netflix (NASDAQ:NFLX) in the red.\nRelated Articles\nPortugal stocks lower at close of trade; PSI 20 down 0.27%\nDenmark stocks higher at close of trade; OMX Copenhagen 20 up 0.55%\nSpain stocks higher at close of trade; IBEX 35 up 1.03%", "external_links": ["https://www.investing.com/analysis/intel-is-20-cheaper-but-the-chip-sector-looks-headed-for-trouble-200344641?utm_source=yahoo&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=yahoo_finance", "https://s.yimg.com/ny/api/res/1.2/CrSxvjKkhW0zuSB7Y7doDQ--~A/YXBwaWQ9aGlnaGxhbmRlcjtzbT0xO3c9NjUwO2g9NDEw/http://media.zenfs.com/en-US/homerun/investing_com_631/1b4657e7f36dfced9bc1739b6578e9e0", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/spain-stocks-higher-at-close-of-trade-ibex-35-up-103-1618023?utm_source=yahoo&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=yahoo_finance", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-